// RFC-018 stage-two footprints for the rpi-pico2 board: real pad geometry
// for every footprint the board's own parts bind. Pad symbols resolve to the
// std pad library (std/pads.cohdl) through the std prelude; pad NUMBERS match
// each bound device's declared pin numbers (RFC-002), so `cohdl build`'s
// E807 pad-consistency check passes. Each comment records the KiCad footprint
// id (or datasheet package) the geometry derives from. The flash (8-XSON 2x3),
// buck-boost (WDFN-10 2.5x2.5), micro-USB (SMD), Schottky (SOD-123W) and
// BOOTSEL switch land patterns were corrected to the datasheet packages in a
// 2026-07 footprint audit (see docs/compliance-report.md). Geometry feeds the
// .kicad_mod / IPC-2581 projection (RFC-015/018); it is nominal land-pattern
// data for partner layout (Quilter), not a placement.

// was: "Package_DFN_QFN:QFN-60-1EP_7x7mm_P0.4mm_EP3.5x3.5mm"
// IPC-7351 name (RFC-021): 60 leads, density N, 0.40mm pitch, 7.00x7.00mm
// body, 3.50x3.50mm exposed pad.
pub footprint QFN60N40P700X700_1EP350X350 {
    pad 1: P_QFN_P04_H at (-3.45mm, -2.8mm)
    pad 2: P_QFN_P04_H at (-3.45mm, -2.4mm)
    pad 3: P_QFN_P04_H at (-3.45mm, -2mm)
